      {
        "id": "p18-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Deduce that $(x+6)(x+4)=x^2+10x+24$ for all values of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Adding the four areas gives $x^2+6x+4x+24=x^2+10x+24$, equal to $(x+6)(x+4)$. The distributive law confirms the identity for all $x$.",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p18-q9-c-worked-area-reason",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The four smaller rectangles together form ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "ABCD",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", so their areas add to its area.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p18-q9-c-worked-area-sum",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{align*}A_{ABCD}&=x^2+6x+4x+24\\\\A_{ABCD}&=x^2+10x+24\\end{align*}",
                    "display": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p18-q9-c-worked-area-product",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "From part b, ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "A_{ABCD}=(x+6)(x+4)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", hence ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(x+6)(x+4)=x^2+10x+24",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p18-q9-c-worked-all-values-reason",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The distributive law confirms this identity for all values of ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ":",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p18-q9-c-worked-distribution",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{align*}(x+6)(x+4)&=x(x+4)+6(x+4)\\\\(x+6)(x+4)&=x^2+4x+6x+24\\\\(x+6)(x+4)&=x^2+10x+24\\end{align*}",
                    "display": true
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
